  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 259 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe upper ridge, stubbornly remains centered near the ArkLaTex \nregion on Saturday as a strong northern stream wave approaches the \nnorthern Rockies and a shortwave approaches from the desert \nsouthwest. This will facilitate a southward progression of a cold \nfront into Kansas on Saturday. This pattern will allow hot \nconditions to persist on Saturday, with a chance of showers and \nthunderstorms returning to north/west Oklahoma by afternoon.\nRain/storm chances increase Saturday night (mainly over northern and \nwestern Oklahoma) with low chances expanding towards the I-44 \ncorridor.\n\nSunday marks the first day of the upcoming pattern change. Latest \nNBM guidance has the cold front reaching northwest Oklahoma on \nSunday morning and the ECMWF/GFS suggest the boundary stalls \nsomewhere over northern Oklahoma. Weak CAA, increased cloudiness, \nand rain/storms will provide for less hot temperatures for most \nareas compared to recent days. Forecast highs range from the upper \n80's (northern OK) to near 100 degrees (southern OK and north TX). \nModel consensus is improving for these temperatures on Sunday, as \nshown by the shrinking boxplot with the 25-75th percentile range \n(reasonable expected high temperatures) having decreased from about \n10 degrees (i.e., a much wider range) the past several runs to about \n5 degrees difference. Unfortunately, the scale has tipped more in \nfavor of warmer temperatures than cooler for Sunday.\n\nThen, a reinforcing front brings enhanced CAA late Sunday and the \nsurface front pushes through central Oklahoma on Sunday night.\nWidespread rain/storms are likely as the boundary progresses \nsouthward. Shower and storms are possible during the day on Sunday, \nespecially over north-central Oklahoma near the front.\nRain chances continue into Monday and diminish from north to south \nduring the day, with high temperatures in the 80's/90's forecast \nboth Monday and Tuesday. There remains large differences in \ntemperatures among ensemble members for next week.\n\nThompson",
